    "input": "What is a savings account?",
    "output": "A savings account is a deposit account where you keep your money with a bank and earn interest on both your deposits and withdrawals. Here’s how it works:\n\n- **Interest:** The bank pays you a regular interest rate on your balance, so your money grows over time.\n- **Minimum Balance:** Many savings accounts require a minimum balance to ensure funds remain available; failing to meet this limit could result in losing access to your account.\n- **FDIC Protection:** Deposits in savings accounts are insured up to $250,000 per depositor, per bank (subject to federal regulations).\n- **Features:** Some accounts offer early withdrawal penalties, higher yields, or additional benefits based on your goals.\n\nAt VinBank, we offer savings accounts designed to help you grow your savings safely and efficiently. If you'd like details on our current rates or account options, just let me know!",
